 ('nvidia', 'EV02', 'Its spokesman tells the Times, for the first report: "Jensen\'s interactions with Ms. Huang are not unusual or unexpected. Meetings with customers are part of a C.E.O.\'s job; Jensen talks with thousands of customer executives every year". The Times adds that the company "has said that it complies with the law and that there is no evidence of its chips being smuggled to China", and that the spokesman said China\'s government has "blocked U.S. AI chips, protecting its own industry". CNBC, that day: it says Huang\'s interactions with Megaspeed\'s officials are not unusual and that the chip-diversion allegations about it were "debunked last year"',
  ['man-nyt-1029-01', 'man-nyt-1029-01', 'cnbc-1029-nvidia-responds', 'man-nyt-1029-01', 'man-nyt-1029-01'],
  ['a spokesman for Nvidia, said: “Jensen’s interactions with Ms. Huang are not unusual or unexpected. Meetings with customers are part of a C.E.O.’s job; Jensen talks with thousands of customer executives every year.”', 'Meetings with customers are part of a C.E.O.’s job; Jensen talks with thousands of customer executives every year.', 'interactions with its officials are not unusual, because he speaks with thousands of customers every year', 'Nvidia has said that it complies with the law and that there is no evidence of its chips being smuggled to China.', 'China’s government has “blocked U.S. AI chips, protecting its own industry.”']),
