 ('board', 'EV30', 'Meets to discuss removing Huang. CNBC, from a person familiar with the matter: it decided that night to oust him and made the decision official the next morning',
  ['sw-cnbccom-09'],
  ["Nvidia's board decided last night to oust longtime CEO Jensen Huang, a person familiar with the matter told CNBC.\nThe person, who spoke on the condition of anonymity, said sentiment quickly turned after the report of a second alleged affair.\nThe team worked late into the night on its communications strategy and made an official decision this morning, before naming Kress as interim CEO, the person added."]),
 ('board', 'EV31', 'Names Kress interim chief, Jones chair; begins a search for a permanent chief, for which it "will consider internal and external candidates" (announced Nov 12; the company\'s filing dates Jones\'s appointment to Nov 11 and gives no day for Kress\'s). The release says Kress keeps her duties as chief financial officer and that results will be reported on Nov 17 "as previously scheduled". Quartz reports, crediting the company, that Jones "will direct the search for a permanent CEO"',
  ['sw-tomshardwarecom-06', 'man-cd8c08517fc7', 'man-cd8c08517fc7', 'man-cd8c08517fc7', 'sw-gizmodocom-10', 'sw-qzcom-19', 'sw-nvidianewsnvidiacom-02', 'sw-nvidianewsnvidiacom-02', 'sw-qzcom-19'],
  ['The Board is initiating a search for a permanent Chief Executive Officer and will consider internal and external candidates', 'On November 11, 2026, the Board appointed Harvey C. Jones, age 73, as Chair of the Board', 'to serve as interim Chief Executive', 'Press Release, dated November 12, 2026', 'Colette Kress, Nvidia’s chief financial officer since 2013, will serve as interim CEO while retaining her CFO duties.', "Harvey C. Jones, who previously led Synopsys $SNPS , is Nvidia 's first board chair and will direct the search for a permanent CEO, which will consider candidates from inside and outside the company, Nvidia said.", 'NVIDIA will report its third-quarter fiscal 2027 financial results on Tuesday, November 17, at approximately 1:20 p.m. PT, as previously scheduled, followed by its earnings call at 2 p.m. PT.', 'The Board is initiating a search for a permanent Chief Executive Officer and will consider internal and external candidates', 'will direct the search for a permanent CEO']),
