 ('commerce', '2026-11-12', 'Politico reports, on the evening of Nov 12, that several people with knowledge of the department\'s operations question whether the under secretary who heads its export bureau "could reasonably shoulder the blame for decisions that ultimately rested with Lutnick, who they say maintained unusually tight control over his subordinates"; a former department official says of the under secretary: "He doesn\'t make any decisions without Lutnick\'s expressed written consent". In a statement, a spokesperson for the bureau says the two "have a strong working relationship, and both are honored to serve under President Trump to his vision to Make America Great Again". The page gives the practice no dates',
  ['ms-fin-yahoo-politico-friendship', 'ms-fin-yahoo-politico-friendship', 'ms-fin-yahoo-politico-friendship', 'ms-fin-yahoo-politico-friendship', 'ms-fin-yahoo-politico-friendship'],
  ["But several people with knowledge of the department's operations questioned whether Kessler could reasonably shoulder the blame for decisions that ultimately rested with Lutnick, who they say maintained unusually tight control over his subordinates.", '"He doesn\'t make any decisions without Lutnick\'s expressed written consent," the official added.', 'said a former Commerce Department official', 'In a statement, a BIS spokesperson said Lutnick and Kessler "have a strong working relationship, and both are honored to serve under President Trump to his vision to Make America Great Again."', 'PUBLISHED: 2026-11-13T00:55:10Z']),
